[stderr] +  save storage, UI selection state, account profiles, or network state.
[stderr] +- **Verification:** Unit tests show invalid commands do not mutate state,
[stderr] +  expected-revision mismatch rejects stale intent, and repeated interaction IDs
[stderr] +  do not produce an extra durable transition.
[stderr] +- **Acceptance evidence:** Versioned type/interface reference, invariant-test
[stderr] +  report, and rejection/idempotency fixtures.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### FDN-06 — Define the local persistence and recovery protocol
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- **Scope / target:** Shared save schema/protocol with a Web local-storage
[stderr] +  adapter; installed PWA uses the same browser-origin data independently of
[stderr] +  cache lifecycle.
[stderr] +- **Bounded outcome:** A schema contract specifies immutable revisions,
[stderr] +  checksums, validated current pointer, last-known-good retention, quarantine,
[stderr] +  settings separation, deletion confirmation, and pure ordered migrations.
[stderr] +- **Dependencies:** FDN-03 and FDN-05; approved browser storage API/quota and
[stderr] +  save-support retention policy.
[stderr] +- **Owns:** `src/core/save/{schema,compatibility,migrations}/`;
[stderr] +  `src/platform/web/persistence/`; `tests/{core,platform}/**/*save*`; save and
[stderr] +  recovery documentation.
[stderr] +- **Does not own:** Cloud sync, account-linked saves, content import/export,
[stderr] +  PWA cache records, or a guarantee after user/browser storage eviction.
[stderr] +- **Verification:** Fault-injection fixtures cover interrupted write, checksum
[stderr] +  failure, malformed/unsupported migration, quota/permission failure,
[stderr] +  quarantine, retry, and selected-slot deletion; every supported predecessor
[stderr] +  fixture migrates once without modifying its original bytes.
[stderr] +- **Acceptance evidence:** Save-state diagram, schema compatibility table,
[stderr] +  fixtures, and passing fault/migration report showing retained valid revision.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### FDN-07 — Bound the deferred identity contract
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- **Scope / target:** Explicit P0 exclusion shared by Web and PWA; no identity
[stderr] +  adapter is built.
[stderr] +- **Bounded outcome:** The domain and storage interfaces prove no player
[stderr] +  account identifier, authentication token, remote profile, or sync authority
[stderr] +  is needed for an offline campaign; future identity integration requirements
[stderr] +  are recorded as a decision gate.
[stderr] +- **Dependencies:** FDN-03, FDN-05; explicit product/privacy/security/vendor
[stderr] +  approval before any connected identity work.
[stderr] +- **Owns:** Architecture/privacy decision record and contract tests asserting
[stderr] +  local-save interfaces require only local slot identity.
[stderr] +- **Does not own:** Sign-up, sign-in, guest accounts, OAuth, session handling,
[stderr] +  cloud sync, remote deletion, or support identity lookups.
[stderr] +- **Verification:** Static/dependency scan finds no account/token fields or
[stderr] +  network identity client in P0 foundation modules; local campaign start/save/
[stderr] +  resume fixture runs with no identity input.
[stderr] +- **Acceptance evidence:** Recorded P0 exclusion, future-approval checklist
[stderr] +  (identity provider, consent, outage, retention/deletion, support, conflict),
[stderr] +  and scan/test output.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### FDN-08 — Bound the deferred authorization contract
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- **Scope / target:** Explicit P0 exclusion shared by Web and PWA; browser
[stderr] +  profile control is not presented as authorization.
[stderr] +- **Bounded outcome:** The contracts state that P0 has no server resource or
[stderr] +  role boundary; future authorization must be server-enforced, least-privilege,
[stderr] +  authenticated per request, auditable, rate-limited, and resilient to outage.
[stderr] +- **Dependencies:** FDN-07 and explicit approval for a server resource and
[stderr] +  identity policy.
[stderr] +- **Owns:** Security/architecture decision record and negative contract tests
[stderr] +  that domain commands do not accept client-asserted role/permission fields.
[stderr] +- **Does not own:** Roles, permissions, administration, moderation, player
[stderr] +  safety, purchase entitlement, server APIs, or client-side permission checks.
[stderr] +- **Verification:** Type/interface scan confirms no authorization fields in
[stderr] +  P0 commands/snapshots; negative fixture rejects or cannot construct a
[stderr] +  client-supplied privilege claim.
[stderr] +- **Acceptance evidence:** P0 authorization-exclusion statement, future
[stderr] +  service authorization checklist, and passing negative test/scan report.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### FDN-09 — Build the layered deterministic test harness
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- **Scope / target:** Shared unit/content/integration harness; Web adapter
[stderr] +  checks; PWA lifecycle browser tests only after service-worker work exists.
[stderr] +- **Bounded outcome:** Test conventions and fixtures make deterministic domain,
[stderr] +  content validation, persistence fault injection, application integration,
[stderr] +  and browser-change coverage independently runnable with isolated data and no
[stderr] +  real services.
[stderr] +- **Dependencies:** FDN-01–FDN-06; FDN-07–FDN-08 exclusion fixtures; approved
[stderr] +  browser/device matrix and performance budgets for final target claims.
[stderr] +- **Owns:** Test-runner configuration; fixture factories; deterministic RNG/
[stderr] +  clock controls; `tests/{core,content,platform,app}/`; test guidance; reserved
[stderr] +  `supervisor/browser/tests/changes/` conventions.
[stderr] +- **Does not own:** Final game feature assertions, production telemetry,
[stderr] +  performance-budget values, or a smoke spec before a browser-facing feature
[stderr] +  has an implemented surface.
[stderr] +- **Verification:** One command runs each test layer; a deliberately failing
[stderr] +  fixture is detected; fixtures cannot write to a real player slot; repeated
[stderr] +  run produces identical core result/event data.
[stderr] +- **Acceptance evidence:** Test command matrix, fixture-isolation proof,
[stderr] +  deterministic-run comparison, and documented mapping from later contract IDs
[stderr] +  to their unit/integration/browser evidence.
