[stderr] +## Purpose and use
[stderr] +
[stderr] +This is the authoring input for later implementation runbooks. Each record is
[stderr] +an atomic, independently reviewable outcome; it is not authority to choose an
[stderr] +engine, vendor, remote service, or production browser matrix. A later runbook
[stderr] +must name its contract ID, preserve its ownership boundary, and either resolve
[stderr] +the listed decision gate or stop before work that depends on it.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The P0 product remains a client-side, offline, single-player web/PWA campaign.
[stderr] +`Shared` denotes work used by both responsive web and installed PWA. `Web`
[stderr] +denotes browser-only work; `PWA` denotes a service-worker/install adaptation.
[stderr] +No contract below creates account, sync, multiplayer, commerce, analytics, or
[stderr] +live-service functionality.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Contract record conventions
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- **Implementation ID** is stable and must be cited by dependent runbooks.
[stderr] +- **Owns** gives the sole initial owner of files and durable data. Paths are
[stderr] +  planned paths until FDN-01 has an approved framework.
[stderr] +- **Does not own** prevents adjacent work from being pulled forward.
[stderr] +- **Acceptance evidence** is the artifact a supervisor can inspect after the
[stderr] +  stated verification passes.
[stderr] +- A decision gate is a blocking approval, not a default that an author may
[stderr] +  silently select.
